# An allowlist, not a blocklist. Everything is excluded and only what the image
# genuinely needs is added back.
#
# A blocklist fails open: the day someone adds a file holding a hostname or a key,
# it ships inside a published layer unless a pattern happened to anticipate it. An
# allowlist fails closed — a new file is absent from the build until someone names
# it here, and a missing file breaks the build loudly rather than leaking quietly.
*

!gpodsync/
!manage.py
!requirements.txt
!docker-entrypoint.sh

# Re-exclude anything that could ride along inside the directories above.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.env*
**/*.sqlite3*
